Message-ID: <-cF-RYSKoH4.F7XSKbYtBwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <-cF-RYSKoH4.Yfi6CmxiBQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <-cF-RYSKoH4.Yfi6CmxiBQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/-cF-RYSKoH4/m/F7XSKbYtBwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

when using copy, the hyperparameters of 'idx' will also be copied. the
scaling infront of the copy, beta, can be controlled if there are more
copies, using the 'same.as <http://same.as>' argument

f(i, model="iid") +
f(j, copy="i", hyper = list(beta = list(fixed=FALSE))) +
f(k, copy="i", same.as <http://same.as>='j')

meanig that the 'beta' for the 'k' copy, is set to the same (as, point
to the same address) as as the 'beta' for the 'j' copy.

H

