Hello

I've been trying to fit simple spde model like below

y ~ N(mu, sigma^2)

mu = covariates*beta + GRF

And I have been facing with two issues

1. Underestimated Gaussian precision
2. Uncertainty measure for the estimated parameter values are all 'zero'.

In fact, the posterior mean of range, kappa, or tau values are similar to the truth - but they all have essentially zero standard deviation.

----------
Fixed effects:
                          mean      sd        0.025quant      0.5quant       0.975quant   mode      kld
ln_totalpop      0.7983   1e-04      0.7981             0.7983          0.7986          0.7983    0

Random effects:
Name   Model
 i   SPDE2 model

Model hyperparameters:
                                                                        mean                       sd            0.025quant       0.5quant     0.975quant       mode
Precision for the Gaussian observations        74.0095                   0.0026     74.0025             74.0088       74.7653         74.0105
Theta1 for i                                                      0.8912                     0.0000     0.8911                0.8912        0.9013          0.8912
Theta2 for i                                                      0.2361                     0.0000     0.2358               0.2361        0.2362           0.2361

Expected number of effective parameters(std dev): 35.71(0.00)
Number of equivalent replicates : 1.624

Deviance Information Criterion (DIC) ...: 1811.45
Effective number of parameters .........: 35.66

Marginal log-Likelihood:  -1883.40
Posterior marginals for linear predictor and fitted values computed
---------------

I know it usually needs to look into the entire code, but can anyone give me a crude sense what is going on here?

Thanks a lot!!

Munji

